question:
Two shaded quarter-circles, each with a radius of 4 units, are formed in the 4 by 8 rectangular region shown. What is the area of the non-shaded region, in square units? Express the area in the form $a-b\pi$ where $a$ and $b$ are integers.

[asy]

size(4cm,4cm);

pair A,B,C,D,a,b,X;

A=(0,0);
B=(8,0);
C=(8,4);
D=(0,4);

X=(4,4);

draw(A--B--C--D--A);

a=(3,1.5);

fill((A..a..X--D--A--cycle),gray);

draw(A..a..X);

b=(5,1.5);

fill((B..b..X--C--B--cycle),gray);

draw(B..b..X);

label("$8$",midpoint(A--B),S);
label("$4$",midpoint(B--C),E);

[/asy]

gemma3_partial_cot_response:
The area of the non-shaded region is the area of the rectangle minus the area of the two shaded quarter-circles. Therefore, the area of the non-shaded region is $32 - 8\pi$.

Thus, the area of the non-shaded region is $32 - 8\pi$ square units.

\boxed{32-8\pi}

