$$R(-5) = a(-5)^2 - b = 6$$
Now we have two equations:
$$\begin{cases} 1 = a + b \\ 6 = 25a - b \end{cases}$$
Solving this system of linear equations, we get $a = 3$ and $b = 4$. Therefore, the remainder when $x^3$ is divided by $x^2 + 5x + 1$ is $3x + 4$.
