The area of the square is $s^2$. The area of the octagon is the area of the square minus the area of the four triangles. Therefore, the area of the octagon is $s^2 - \frac{2}{9} s^2 = \frac{7}{9} s^2$.
Since $s = 27$, the area of the octagon is $\frac{7}{9} (27^2) = \frac{7}{9} (729) = 7 \times 81 = 567$ square centimeters.

