We are asked to add $175_{9} + 714_{9} + 61_9$ in base $9$.
We can add the numbers vertically, carrying over when the sum of the digits in a column is greater than or equal to $9$.
\begin{align*} \label{eq:1} 175_9 \\ 714_9 \\ + \quad 61_9 \\ \hline \end{align*}
In the rightmost column, we have $5 + 4 + 1 = 10 = 1 \cdot 9 + 1$, so we write down $1$ and carry-over $1$.
\begin{align*} 1 \\ 175_9 \\ 714_9 \\ + \quad 61_9 \\ \hline \quad 1_9 \end{align*}
In the next column, we have $7 + 1 + 6 + 1 = 15 = 1 \cdot 9 + 6$, so we write down $6$ and carry-over $1$.
\begin{align*} 11 \\ 175_9 \\ 714_9 \\ + \quad 61_9 \\ \hline \quad 61_9 \end{align*}
In the next column, we have $1 + 7 + 1 = 9 = 1 \cdot 9 + 0$, so we write down $0$ and carry-over $1$.
\begin{align*} 111 \\ 175_9 \\ 714_9 \\ + \quad 61_9 \\ \hline 061_9 \end{align*}
Then we write down the carried-over $1$.
\begin{align*} 111 \\ 175_9 \\ 714_9 \\ + \quad 61_9 \\ \hline 1061_9 \end{align*}
Thus, we have $175_9 + 714_9 + 61_9 = 1061_9$.

We can also convert the numbers to base $10$, add them, and then convert the result back to base $9$.
\begin{align*} 175_9 &= 1 \cdot 9^2 + 7 \cdot 9^1 + 5 \cdot 9^0 = 1 \cdot 81 + 7 \cdot 9 + 5 \cdot 1 = 81 + 63 + 5 = 149 \\ 714_9 &= 7 \cdot 9^2 + 1 \cdot 9^1 + 4 \cdot 9^0 = 7 \cdot 81 + 1 \cdot 9 + 4 \cdot 1 = 567 + 9 + 4 = 580 \\ 61_9 &= 6 \cdot 9^1 + 1 \cdot 9^0 = 6 \cdot 9 + 1 \cdot 1 = 54 + 1 = 55 \end{align*}
The sum in base $10$ is $149 + 580 + 55 = 784$.
Now we convert $784$ to base $9$.
\begin{align*} 784 \div 9 &= 87 \text{ remainder } 1 \\ 87 \div 9 &= 9 \text{ remainder } 6 \\ 9 \div 9 &= 1 \text{ remainder } 0 \\ 1 \div 9 &= 0 \text{ remainder } 1 \end{align*}
Reading the remainders from bottom to top, we have $784 = 1061_9$.

Final Answer: The final answer is $\boxed{1061_9}$

