Let the given matrices be $A = \begin{pmatrix} 3 & 1 & 0 \\ -7 & 4 & 2 \\ 0 & 5 & -1 \end{pmatrix}$ and $v = \begin{pmatrix} 4 \\ -1 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix}$. We want to compute $Av$.
The product $Av$ is given by
\begin{align*} Av &= \begin{pmatrix} 3 & 1 & 0 \\ -7 & 4 & 2 \\ 0 & 5 & -1 \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 4 \\ -1 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix} \\ &= \begin{pmatrix} 3(4) + 1(-1) + 0(-2) \\ -7(4) + 4(-1) + 2(-2) \\ 0(4) + 5(-1) + (-1)(-2) \end{pmatrix} \\ &= \begin{pmatrix} 12 - 1 + 0 \\ -28 - 4 - 4 \\ 0 - 5 + 2 \end{pmatrix} \\ &= \begin{pmatrix} 11 \\ -36 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix}. \end{align*}

Thus,
\[\begin{pmatrix} 3 & 1 & 0 \\ -7 & 4 & 2 \\ 0 & 5 & -1 \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 4 \\ -1 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 11 \\ -36 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix}.\]

\boxed{\begin{pmatrix} 11 \\ -36 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix}}

